  "goodToKnow": "Das Schuljahr is the school year. In Germany it's divided into two Halbjahre, each ending with a Zeugnis (report). Summer holidays are staggered by state so not everyone hits the Autobahn at once, so the new Schuljahr starts anywhere from late July to mid-September. First-graders get a Schultüte, a big cone of sweets and school supplies, on their first day. Das Schuljahr wiederholen means to repeat a year."
